# What the image build reads is short: the root cargo manifests,
# `.cargo/config.toml`, `rust-toolchain.toml`, `crates/`, `tasks/` (only so the
# root workspace's member list resolves), the root JS manifests, `packages/`,
# `scripts/` and `types/`. Everything named here is large, host-specific, or a
# build output that has to be regenerated inside the image.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare name matches only at the context root; `**/` is what
# reaches nested directories.

# Rust build trees. The wasm client is excluded from the root workspace and so
# has one of its own.
target
crates/agent-inject-wasm-client/target

# Front-end installs and output: reinstalled and rebundled in the image.
**/node_modules
dist

# Where the wasm and its glue land, plus the hash of this machine's last build.
# All gitignored and therefore present in every working checkout. Copying any of
# them in would let a stale host build become the image's wasm, which the
# content-addressed name in `scripts/wasm-asset.ts` exists to prevent.
packages/agent-inject-wasm/src/path.ts
packages/agent-inject-wasm/src/glue

# Nothing in the image build reads git metadata, and `cargo task
# publish-web-image` resolves the tag on the host before calling docker.
.git
.gitignore

# Not part of the web app.
docs
skills
deploy
.claude
.github
README.md
LICENSE
clippy.toml
rustfmt.toml

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# Never send secrets, whatever else moves above.
**/.env
**/.env.*
